{
 "_source": "pvpoke src/data/rankings/all/overall/rankings-1500.json (great) and rankings-2500.json (ultra) at pvpoke commit 9ad871c3e, 2026-09-08 -- the vintage gopvpsim's rankings cache held while the replay blobs these tests read were dived and while tests/test_deep_dive_brief.py was written (2026-09-11 .. 2026-09-13).",
 "_why": "build_opp_meta_ranks reads the LIVE rankings, so every PvPoke refresh renumbers the ranks this module pins AND re-selects the rank-gated content the module asserts about (RANK_GATE = 50). The 2026-09-15 refresh renumbered Annihilape 30 -> 31 and moved Charjabug 60 -> 41, and the newly-eligible Charjabug cells deleted Melmetal's floor outright -- 17 tests here failed on a data refresh with no code change. Pinning the vintage keeps the oracle numbers comparable to the blobs they were computed from.",
 "_order": "score-descending exactly as PvPoke published it; rank = index + 1.",
 "_contents": "speciesId only: build_opp_meta_ranks reads nothing else from a rankings entry, and a consumer that wants more (a moveset, a score) raises KeyError here instead of silently reading a different vintage.",
